Chapter 10
Scarlet doesn't seem as pleased by the idea as me.
Scarlet: Something like that can't just be undone. I will still have to live with the fact that at one point, I killed that bastard. I can't just forget about that so easily.
(t): She has a point. Still, it would be devastating to have to go through that a second time.
Me: I'm sure we can at least try to—
I can't even finish my sentence before something grabs me by the neck.
Scarlet's eyes widen and she stands up abruptly, knocking her teacup from the table.
Scarlet: Who are you? How did you get in here? Amelie! Call the guards!
A person wearing a black cloak stands behind me.
(t): What's with this person? They just appeared behind me so suddenly. And I can't shake the feeling that I will be killed if I just do so much as to move.
I'm paralysed with fear and don't dare to even utter a word.
The presence of the person behind me comes off as dark and menacing.
I can even see it visually, as some kind of mist, forming itself around the person.
(t): Ew… It's like some sort of black goo is oozing out of this person. Could this be some kind of aura that showcases their power?
???: Do not fret, it is futile. I will be taking the new Sustainer. I'll deal with you at a later time.
Scarlet: Stop! Who do you think you are, barging in like this?!
While Amelie and the guards arrive, Scarlet lunges forward, reaching out her hand towards me.
???: I told you, there is no use.
I try to grab Scarlet's outstretched hand, but then the intruder's hand covers my face and pulls me backwards with an immense force.
(t): Ow!
Scarlet: No! {playerName}!
I hear Scarlet shouting, but at the same time I feel myself getting dragged into a dark abyss, together with the unknown person.
(t): I'm getting kidnapped! Scarlet! Help!
The fear is taking over my body and I feel myself shaking like a leaf.
???: At last, we're one step closer to our goal.
(t): What does that mean? And who are they? Why do they need me?
A lot of questions are running through my mind, but more than that, the feeling of being separated from Scarlet stings in my chest.
(t): I hope that at least she is safe.
I remember her expression just before I got dragged here. It's so vivid in my mind.
(t): I don't want to be drowning in this darkness. I want to be with Scarlet right now and know for sure that she's safe. Who knows if more of these weird people showed up after I vanished.
The moment I finish that thought, I see twinkling stars appear in the distance, illuminating this suffocating darkness and slowly inching closer to me.
(t): This is familiar! I saw this when we shifted to the past!
I begin to struggle, trying to free myself from the person's grasp.
???: What? Cease this behaviour! I must confine you here!
Me: Ugh, let me go!
I muster up all my strength until suddenly, I feel something tingle in my hands.
(t): What's this feeling? This is new.
Before I can think any more about it, a massive explosion bursts out of my hands. It separates me from the mysterious person and I manage to escape into the familiar stars.
???: Agh! Get back here!
The shouts of the cloaked person grow fainter as they disappear into the distant darkness I left behind.
MINIGAME
(t): Did I make it?
That explosion seems to have taken a toll on me, because the next thing I know, I black out completely.
When I open my eyes, I see the ceiling of my familiar bedroom in my apartment.
(t): Huh? I'm back? Or was that all just a bad dream?
I sigh and ponder all the events that happened while we were in the past.
(t): I hope Scarlet is safe.
The more I think about it, the more confused I feel.
(t): I found out a lot about her but I still feel like I want to know more.
CHOICE OPTION 1: This feeling… could it be?
(t): What's wrong with me? Even though I know she's a vampire and also my boss, I can't stop worrying about her. I don't know about the people in the bunker either. What's the deal with them?
I realise that my mind has been occupied with Scarlet lately.
(t): No way, it can't be… or can it?
I can't take my mind off her and each time her face appears in my thoughts, it's tugging on my heart strings.
(t): Am I… falling for her?
I feel the heat rising to my face.
(t): No, that can't be! She's my boss! And a vampire! And she can be so mean at work.
A chill runs down my spine.
(t): Wait, could it be that I'm into that?!
Then the image of her eating breakfast together with me and smiling during that time pops into my mind. And I suddenly notice this warm, fuzzy feeling.
(t): Oh, I guess there is some attraction I can't deny. What do I do?
I try to calm down and come to terms with my new realisation.
(t): Maybe I just got a bit overwhelmed, maybe a distraction would be good. But still, I'm worried…
CHOICE OPTION 2: She's a vampire.
Until recently I probably wouldn't even have believed that that is possible.
But after what I went through, with all of the stuff about the Interdimensional Spirits and the woman that appeared in my dreams before, it doesn't seem so unbelievable anymore.
(t): Right, the Interdimensional Spirits. With all the work and stuff that's happened, I almost forgot about that.
(t): Now that I think about it, that cloaked person might have been one of those Spirits.
(t): And they called me the new Sustainer. I wonder what's up with that. But those Spirits seem way scarier than my vampire boss.
I feel no fear when I think about Scarlet, maybe because she reassured me that vampires don't normally attack humans for their blood.
(t): Apart from her cold attitude at work, she doesn't scare me at all.
I feel a weird feeling in my chest.
(t): I even kind of… miss her. I wonder if Scarlet is safe. I hope so.
CHOICE OPTION 3: The people from the bunker.
(t): She still hasn't told me more about the people that were with her in the bunker.
(t): Instead, she revealed her past of becoming a princess and murdering her ex to me.
I wonder if the people she called her family know about her being a vampire too.
(t): Surely they do, if she trusts them, no? But they called her “boss”.
Then, something dawns on me.
(t): What if they are also vampires? That would explain their mysteriousness to some degree.
CONTINUE HERE AFTER CHOICE OPTIONS
My thoughts are interrupted by the door bell.
I look at the clock. It's 8 in the morning.
(t): Who could this be at this hour?
A wave of fear comes over me.
(t): It can't be one of those cloaked Spirits, can it?
I try to shake the thought of the Interdimensional Spirits and get out of bed.
As I make my way to the door, I realise that I'm late for work.
(t): But maybe Scarlet isn't even here, so then it doesn't count, right?
I open the door and am surprised to see some familiar faces.
(t): It's the three guys that joined us back in the bunker!
Me: Hello, can I help you?
???: Heya! You doin' ok? Oh right, we met before, in the bunker, rember?
(t): It's the man that called Scarlet “boss”.
Me: Um, yes. What brings you guys here?
???: Ahem, Ray. We should introduce ourselves first.
One of the other guys tugs on the arm of, supposedly, Ray.
Ray: Hm? Ah, sorry sorry. You're so right! I'm Ray, nice to meet'cha again! This right here is Lucius, we call him Lu. He's a bit shy but he'll warm up to ya in no time.
He points to the one tugging on his arm. Lu partly hides his body behind ray.
Lu: Hi…
Ray: And last but not least, this is Seth. Also not a man of many words, but I'll make up for it!
